      'Temporary missions in France or a third State: up to 10 days a year count inside the 40%, only as far as they fit after ordinary telework. Part-time or part-year: the 10 days are reduced in proportion and rounded up. Any excess mission day in France ends the 1983 regime, and any in a third state counts toward the 45. BorderDay cannot tell France from a third state, so treat every excess mission day as a risk. Sources: ESTV practical sheet; impots.gouv.fr 1983 interpretative agreement.',
